Agent: You decided on a Pothos for your new home plant. Good choice — it’s beginner-friendly and forgiving.

Quick recap and care tips:
- Light: bright, indirect light is best; will tolerate low light but grows slower. Avoid strong direct sun.
- Water: water when the top 1" (2–3 cm) of soil is dry. Typically every 1–2 weeks depending on humidity/temperature. Don’t let it sit in water.
- Soil & pot: well-draining potting mix and a pot with drainage holes.
- Temperature & humidity: prefers 65–85°F (18–29°C) and moderate humidity; tolerates typical home conditions.
- Fertilizer: balanced houseplant fertilizer about once a month during spring/summer.
- Pruning & training: trim long/viney stems to encourage bushiness; you can train vines on a trellis or let them trail.
- Propagation: very easy — cut a stem below a node and root in water or soil.
- Common issues: yellowing leaves = overwatering; brown tips = low humidity or salt build-up. Pothos are toxic to pets if chewed — keep out of reach.
- Popular varieties: Golden, Marble Queen, Neon — let me know if you want a specific look.

